.TH BILIBILIVE 1 "2026-11-21" "bilibilive 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bilibilive \- native Bilibili streaming studio, CLI and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bilibilive
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
bilibilive manages Bilibili live rooms, OBS integration, PK media and native
automation. The zgpui desktop, CLI, MCP server and zuse host use the same
operation schemas and application dispatcher.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui [--demo] [--listen ADDRESS]
Open the native desktop. Demo mode uses offline sample data and never invokes
account or broadcast operations. Explicit --listen starts a loopback API that
shares the window's account and media session. Demo mode rejects a listener.
.TP
.B login [--name NAME]
Generate a login QR code and poll until authentication, expiry or timeout.
.TP
.B status, start, stop, stream
Read room status, start a broadcast, stop a broadcast, or read an existing
stream endpoint. Reading a stream endpoint does not start a room.
.TP
.B room, area, account, obs, pk, rtc, danmaku, convert
Run a named operation. Use
.B schema
for the complete operation and argument catalogue.
.TP
.B call METHOD --args JSON
Invoke an operation with a JSON object. Use
.B --args -
to read the object from standard input.
.TP
.B rtc preview-local
Keep a local OBS picture preview running in the foreground until Ctrl-C.
Audio monitoring requires an explicit --arg audio=true. The companion OBS
capture plugin and FFplay are required.
.TP
.B schema
Print all registered operation names and JSON input schemas.
.TP
.B doctor
Print local application and dependency capabilities.
.TP
.B mcp
Serve MCP over standard input/output. Diagnostic messages go to stderr.
.TP
.B serve [--listen 127.0.0.1:18779]
Serve local HTTP MCP and control endpoints. The listener requires a loopback
address. Requests require a Bearer token except for the health endpoint.
.TP
.B zuse run FILE
Preflight and execute a bounded native zuse program.
.TP
.B zuse check FILE
Parse and validate the complete program without executing operations.
.TP
.B zuse eval SOURCE
Preflight and execute an inline zuse program.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config-dir PATH
Use an isolated preferences directory.
.TP
.B --endpoint URL
Dispatch CLI operations, login and zuse to an existing local session using
/api/call. Supply its token through BILIBILIVE_API_TOKEN. The URL must be an
HTTP origin with a literal loopback IP, without credentials, path, query or
fragment. The client disables proxies and redirects. The target process owns
the account and configuration; set --config-dir on that process at startup.
.TP
.B --cookie-file PATH
Read temporary credentials from a file. A path of - reads standard input.
.TP
.B --read-only
Reject operations that change application or remote platform state.
.TP
.B --show-secrets
Explicitly include returned stream keys in command output. Default CLI
presentation redacts credential fields.
.TP
.B --json
Print compact JSON.
.TP
.B --arg KEY=VALUE
Add a typed JSON operation argument. May be repeated.
.TP
.B --compat
Enable the legacy unauthenticated /api/startLive and /api/stopLive routes on
the loopback HTTP listener.
.TP
.B --help
Display commands and options.
.TP
.B --version
Display the package version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BILIBILIVE_COOKIE
Temporary session Cookie header, instead of an OS-stored account credential.
.TP
.B BILIBILIVE_OBS_PASSWORD
Temporary OBS WebSocket password.
.TP
.B BILIBILIVE_API_TOKEN
HTTP Bearer token, at least 24 characters. If omitted, the local server
generates a token and prints it on startup. An --endpoint client requires
the target server's token in this variable.
.TP
.B BILIBILIVE_GUI_FRAMES
Exit the desktop after the specified positive number of rendered frames;
intended for isolated GUI verification.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bilibilive login --name daily
bilibilive room update --title 'Today' --area 371
bilibilive start --protocol srt --strategy fallback
bilibilive stream --show-secrets
bilibilive call obs.configure --args -
bilibilive mcp --read-only
bilibilive zuse check studio.zuse
bilibilive zuse run studio.zuse
bilibilive gui --listen 127.0.0.1:18779
bilibilive --endpoint http://127.0.0.1:18779 rtc status
bilibilive rtc preview-local --arg audio=true --arg volume=40
.fi
.SH NOTES
Platform permissions and identity checks remain controlled by Bilibili.
Strict SRT can leave a successfully started room without a usable SRT
endpoint; that result explicitly reports the already-live room.
The full StartLive compatibility and verification matrix accompanies the
source distribution.
.PP
RTC, preview, event connections and OBS observers belong to their creating
process. Ordinary local CLI calls close these resources on exit. Use the same
--endpoint for a sequence of stateful media commands, or use the foreground
preview/watch commands. HTTP MCP at /mcp shares the same persistent session.
